Z||000000||WisconsinGT||02-04-2000||01:15 PM||||I just bought the Pioneer 3 ways for the front of my 88GT. Can someone tell me what I need for connections. I would rather not splice into the factory wires. Also, where do I get the adaptors? Thanks||||reg||1
Z||000001||Raydar||02-04-2000||01:32 PM||||Crutchfield &lt; <A HREF="http://www.crutchfield.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.crutchfield.com</A>  &gt; has the appropriate connectors. Their 800 # is on the web page. Just give them a call. They're not expensive. (Seems like they might have actually been free, --sort of a goodwill kinda thing.) They are good folks to deal with. Got my CD changer in two(!) days. When you wire your speakers, make sure that they are wired with the same polarity as the originals. <p>[This message has been edited by Raydar (edited 02-04-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||DRH||02-04-2000||01:34 PM||||Any place that does installations should carry the adapter harness. Maybe Best Buy???<P>I haven't actually bought any... I am assuming the Fiero uses a "common" GM plug for the speakers and not some one-of-a-kind design.||||reg||1
